-- title:
--   Complete splitting forces trivial residue extension
-- statement:
--   Let $F'/F$ be an extension of fields with $F'$ finite-dimensional as an $F$-vector space, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a valuation subring of $F$. Let $\iota$ be a finite index type and let $i \mapsto \mathcal{O}'_i$ be a family of valuation subrings of $F'$ indexed by $\iota$, subject to three hypotheses: the assignment $i \mapsto \mathcal{O}'_i$ is injective, so the members of the family are pairwise distinct; the preimage of each $\mathcal{O}'_i$ under the structure map $F \to F'$ is exactly $\mathcal{O}$, that is, each $\mathcal{O}'_i$ prolongs $\mathcal{O}$; and $[F' : F] \le |\iota|$, the number of members of the family being at least the degree of the extension. Then for every index $i$ and every $x \in \mathcal{O}'_i$ there exists $y \in \mathcal{O}$ such that $x - y$ (the image of $y$ in $F'$ being understood) lies in the set of non-units of $\mathcal{O}'_i$, i.e. in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}'_i$. Equivalently, the residue field of each $\mathcal{O}'_i$ is generated by the image of the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, so that the residue degree $f(\mathcal{O}'_i/\mathcal{O})$ equals $1$.
--
--   This is the residual half of the standard corollary to the fundamental inequality $\sum_i e_i f_i \le [F':F]$ of valuation theory: if a valuation of $F$ admits at least $[F':F]$ distinct prolongations to $F'$, then each prolongation is unramified with trivial residue extension. It is stated for arbitrary fields and valuation subrings of arbitrary rank, and is used in the proof of [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_prolongation_of_card_roots_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_prolongation_of_card_roots_eq); the argument goes through the simultaneous approximation statement [`ValuationSubring.exists_forall_mem_and_sub_mem_nonunits`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.exists_forall_mem_and_sub_mem_nonunits) for pairwise incomparable valuation subrings.
